version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-29"
abstract: >
  A bi-national, continental analysis of freshwater salinization across the United
  States and Canada. It harmonizes five long-term water-quality networks, quantifies
  multi-decadal trends in six major ions, attributes their drivers with interpretable
  machine learning under spatial cross-validation, fingerprints salt sources with ion
  ratios, classifies stations into salinization regimes, and projects salinization and
  regulatory-threshold exceedance to 2050 under trend, climate, and management scenarios.
